# Each app's Dockerfile builds from the repo root's build context: it copies
# the workspace manifests, the shared packages and the app's own source, then
# installs dependencies inside the image (native modules are platform
# specific, so an install done on the host would not run on the Linux image).
#
# Everything else is excluded — the images only need what they copy.
*
!package.json
!bun.lock
!bunfig.toml
!patches
!packages
!apps

# Exclude the installed dependency trees, the build caches and the local
# artefacts. `node_modules` is excluded everywhere *except* under an app's
# `.next` directory — see the note at the bottom.
**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/coverage
**/.DS_Store
apps/*/.next/cache
apps/*/.next/trace
apps/*/.next/**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/*/dist
out

# Turbopack traces the server's external packages into `.next/node_modules/`
# under content-hashed names (`mongoose-8b99e611e7552af3` and friends), and the
# server requires them by those exact names. Excluding it makes the image fail
# to boot with "Failed to load external module", so it has to ship.
!apps/*/.next/node_modules
